{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/778110-silver-fang-mating-ritual","id":778110,"title":"Silver Fang mating Ritual?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-01T21:53:23-08:00","id":778110,"title":"Silver Fang mating Ritual?","content":"Alright, this was brought up in play to me, I've played a Silver Fang before but when I did I actually came into play with someone else playing my mate, this is the first time that I've had someone become my PC's mate in play. It was mentioned that there's some form of ritual (Either Ritual as in the background or Ritual as in it's just something Silver Fangs do...I'm not sure). <br /> <br /> But apparently when they take a mate they mark them with a bite. <br /> <br /> I skimmed the book but I couldn't see it anywhere listed as something they do. Can anyone point me in the right direction to the book/page that it might be listed in, this'd help so much. Danka","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:00:24-08:00","id":778146,"title":"","content":"Never read something like that. I know of a rite that leads a Silver Fang to the house (or similar dwelling place) the potential best suited mate lives in. The catch being that you don't know if the mate is the bastard child working as housemaid or the daughter of the household, or her little sister whom you have to wait several years for to become of age.<br /> <br /> I found that this rite made all the other mentions of political dealings and intermarriage for power gain kind of unwise. For why defy a rite that if properly executed would bring you the best offspring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:04:46-08:00","id":778149,"title":"","content":"I think you are thinking forsaken on the bite thing. Strikes me as something the storm lords would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:43:03-08:00","id":778401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/778110-silver-fang-mating-ritual?p=778146#post778146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never read something like that. I know of a rite that leads a Silver Fang to the house (or similar dwelling place) the potential best suited mate lives in. The catch being that you don't know if the mate is the bastard child working as housemaid or the daughter of the household, or her little sister whom you have to wait several years for to become of age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeurgh. Not that I am doubting you, Heinrich, but if that is the way the rite works, that is hella stupid. It sounds like the creepyass plotpoint in Twilight when shirtless wereshiftmuffin takes a shine to the newborn baby and claims she is his soulmate.<br /> <br /> I think if I was going to a have a rite like that, one that reveals 'your ideal mate,' it should actually be someone... ideal. A Silver Fang lord isn't really gonna go great with a milkmaid (think of the bloodline!) and 'lol your ideal mate is a 6 year old haha' is mindfryingly dumb. The rite doesn't really work if the 'ideal mate' isn't ideal at all, for one reason or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-02-2015, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T01:39:17-08:00","id":778859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/778110-silver-fang-mating-ritual?p=778401#post778401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeurgh. Not that I am doubting you, Heinrich, but if that is the way the rite works, that is hella stupid. It sounds like the creepyass plotpoint in Twilight when shirtless wereshiftmuffin takes a shine to the newborn baby and claims she is his soulmate.<br /> <br /> I think if I was going to a have a rite like that, one that reveals 'your ideal mate,' it should actually be someone... ideal. A Silver Fang lord isn't really gonna go great with a milkmaid (think of the bloodline!) and 'lol your ideal mate is a 6 year old haha' is mindfryingly dumb. The rite doesn't really work if the 'ideal mate' isn't ideal at all, for one reason or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was exaggerating.<br /> The Rite actually leads to a vision of Falcon carrying the garou to the home of the best suited mate (biologically and spiritually) within a few days away from the caern. Said person probably isn't your soulmate, but the best mate in the limited pool of kinfolk close by. So for the top Silver Fangs it still makes sense to arrange marriages to other top Silver Fangs in septs farther away, while the lower Silver Fangs might use the Rite and hope they aren't lead to a marries woman.<br /> Certainly a partner not yet of age would not be in the pool the Rite chooses from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T02:01:19-08:00","id":778866,"title":"","content":"So it is possible to play someone so screwed up as Charles the 2nd of Spain and not be a metis? Hell yeah!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T04:47:41-08:00","id":778924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/778110-silver-fang-mating-ritual?p=778859#post778859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was exaggerating.<br /> The Rite actually leads to a vision of Falcon carrying the garou to the home of the best suited mate (biologically and spiritually) within a few days away from the caern. Said person probably isn't your soulmate, but the best mate in the limited pool of kinfolk close by. So for the top Silver Fangs it still makes sense to arrange marriages to other top Silver Fangs in septs farther away, while the lower Silver Fangs might use the Rite and hope they aren't lead to a marries woman.<br /> Certainly a partner not yet of age would not be in the pool the Rite chooses from.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's nice to hear something reasonable about the Silver Fangs for a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T06:52:44-08:00","id":778969,"title":"","content":"I think someone has been reading way to many shifter romance novels. That is the only place I have read about mating bites...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T09:07:23-08:00","id":781156,"title":"","content":"Alright cool, thanks folks for the replies. I wasn't sure if it was something that was done in games she played [as she may have been taught this by someone else as well], or if it was something I was unaware of due to a lack of having played Silver Fangs before. So now I know, and knowing is half the battle <i>G.I. Joe!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T13:54:41-08:00","id":781831,"title":"","content":"I think you meant to say.... YOOOOOO, Joe!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":